data_LiMgZrCl_seed_reduced
# REDUCED FIXTURE — pre-registered novel-challenge SEED.
# NOT a novelty claim. The PRD §Scope explicitly classifies
# "Li2.2Mg0.1Zr0.9Cl6" in the Li-Mg-Zr-Cl halide design family as a
# pre-registered generated challenge candidate, NOT as a novelty claim,
# until L6 de-duplication and L2/L1 validation pass. The fixture exists
# so the orchestration layer has a concrete starting structure to
# parameterise the L6 generative loop and the L2 DPA-3+MACE ensemble
# screening — the L7 reasoner is expected to either confirm novelty
# against MP/JARVIS/Alexandria/GNoME/OPTIMADE or pivot to a sibling
# composition.
#
# We choose the host lattice as Li3ZrCl6-style (a known halide
# solid-electrolyte family, e.g. Li3YCl6, Li3InCl6, Li3ZrCl6), space
# group P-3m1 / trigonal, conventional a ≈ 6.51 Å, c ≈ 6.05 Å.
# We embed Mg2+ on one of the M3+ (Zr) sites at fractional occupancy
# 0.1 (here represented as a single ordered Mg site to satisfy fixture
# stoichiometry) with a compensating Li excess.
# The ratio Li2.2 Mg0.1 Zr0.9 Cl6 is approximated in this 14-atom seed
# as: 2 Li + 1 Mg + 1 Zr + 6 Cl = Li2 Mg1 Zr1 Cl6 (ordered fixture
# composition, NOT the exact target stoichiometry). The exact target
# stoichiometry will be reached in the L6 generator's special-quasi-
# random-structure (SQS) expansion phase; this fixture is the seed.
#
# Mark `novelty_status: pending` in the manifest.
#
# Sources:
#   - Asano, T. et al. "Solid Halide Electrolytes with High Lithium-Ion
#     Conductivity for Application in 4 V Class Bulk-Type All-Solid-State
#     Batteries", Adv. Mater. 30(44), 1803075 (2018).
#     DOI: 10.1002/adma.201803075
#   - Park, K.-H. et al. "High-Voltage Superionic Halide Solid Electrolytes
#     for All-Solid-State Li-Ion Batteries", ACS Energy Lett. 5(2),
#     533–539 (2020). DOI: 10.1021/acsenergylett.9b02599
#   - Wang, S. et al. "Lithium chlorides and bromides as promising
#     solid-state chemistries for fast ion conductors with good
#     electrochemical stability", Angew. Chem. Int. Ed. 58(24),
#     8039–8043 (2019). DOI: 10.1002/anie.201901938
_cell_length_a 6.510
_cell_length_b 6.510
_cell_length_c 6.050
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 120.0
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
